    "First/Final Written Warning": {
        "content": "{{>header\r\n    title=(concat warning_type \" Written Warning\")\r\n    department=\"Tactical Firearms Unit\"\r\n}}\r\n\r\nHello **{{officer_name}}**,<br/>\r\n\r\nThis is a 'written warning'. It has been identified that your performance must improve, and it is hoped that this measure will encourage you to take steps towards better performance.<br/><br/>\r\n\r\n<b>Type of Written Warning:<br/>\r\n{{warning_type}}</b><br/><br/>\r\n\r\n<b>Performance area(s) for review:</b><br/>\r\n{{area}}<br/><br/>\r\n\r\n<b>Considerations for improvement:</b><br/>\r\n{{improvement}}<br/><br/>\r\n\r\n<b>Date for review: {{review_date}}</b><br/><br/>\r\n\r\nI need to know your thoughts on what has been discussed above. I also need you to let me know if there is anything or anybody that may be responsible for unsatisfactory performance. I will try my best to support you.<br/><br/>\r\n\r\nPlease remember that this may remain active on your record as an infraction for 3/6 months. If you wish to appeal the warning, you may do so by submitting a helpdesk ticket to Professional Standards or the Chiefs of Department.<br/><br/>\r\n\r\n<b>Regards,</b><br/>\r\n{{sender_rank}} {{sender_name}}<br/>\r\n{{sender_role}}\r\n",
